cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  CTI-RLex: claimant-terminal-invariant robust lexicographic water allocation
message: >-
  If you use this software or either benchmark, please cite both the software and the
  article it accompanies.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.0.1
date-released: "2026-08-29"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22160054
repository-code: "https://github.com/Adilbaygh/CTI-RLex"
abstract: >-
  A linear-programming implementation of claimant-terminal-invariant robust lexicographic
  allocation for lossy multi-source irrigation networks, with two open Utah benchmarks,
  the comparator and sensitivity experiments reported in the accompanying article, and a
  desktop benchmark analyzer.
keywords:
  - irrigation water allocation
  - lexicographic max-min fairness
  - multi-source networks
  - water scarcity
  - robust optimization
  - bounded recourse
  - computational benchmark
